# What must NOT go into the image, and why each line is here.
#
# The build context is sent to the daemon before anything runs, so an entry that
# looks like housekeeping is also the difference between a 200 MB context and a
# 2 GB one on an Uzbek uplink.

# History. Hundreds of megabytes, and it carries every value ever committed —
# including anything that was committed and then removed.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# The file storage backend's default root (`storage_root = ./var/media`). This is
# uploaded media on the developer's laptop. Copying it into the image would ship
# somebody's test audio to production AND shadow the mount point at
# /var/lib/ielts/media if the paths ever coincide.
var/

# Real secrets. `.env` is gitignored, which protects the repository and does
# nothing for the build context — `COPY . .` would put it in a layer that anyone
# who can pull the image can read. `.env.example` is deliberately not excluded:
# it holds no values, and having it in the image means `docker run --rm image cat
# .env.example` answers "what does this need" without a checkout.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The test suite and its scaffolding. Not shipped, per pyproject.toml: "`app` is
# the distribution. The rest of the repo is the repository, not the package."
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# CI-only. `scripts/` holds the gates (`check_migrations.py`, `check_coverage.py`,
# `smoke_workers.py`); none of them runs on the production box, and
# `smoke_workers.py` in particular CREATEs and DROPs databases.
scripts/
openapi/
# …except the contract itself, which the `web` build stage generates the typed
# client from. Excluding the directory outright made `COPY openapi/openapi.yaml`
# fail with "file not found" — a build-context exclusion, not a missing file, and
# the error does not say so.
!openapi/openapi.yaml
docs/
Makefile

# Tool caches. Machine-specific absolute paths, useless in a container, and
# .mypy_cache alone is tens of megabytes.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# A virtualenv from the host is built against the host's libc and the host's
# Python. Copying one in produces an image that imports nothing.
.venv/
venv/

# The deployment files themselves. They configure the image; they are not part
# of it.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.dev.yml
README.md

# NOT the Caddyfile, which used to be on that list with the rest of them and the
# reasoning "a change to it should not invalidate every layer after the COPY".
# True, and irrelevant: the `caddy` stage ends with
#
#     COPY Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# so excluding it does not save a rebuild, it makes the build fail —
# `"/Caddyfile": not found` — and the error blames a missing file rather than
# the exclusion that hid it. Exactly the trap documented twenty lines above for
# `openapi/`, made a second time in the same file. There is no layer after this
# COPY to invalidate; it is the last instruction in the last stage.
#
# `scripts/check_build_definition.py` now fails the build when a path some COPY
# reads is excluded here.

# Frontend build artefacts. `node_modules` is larger than the rest of the context
# put together and the `web` stage runs `npm ci` itself; a copied-in `dist/`
# would silently shadow the one the stage builds.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
